{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/551081-forget-me-not-life-after-un-life","id":551081,"title":"Forget me not, life after un-life","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-11T21:52:39-07:00","id":551081,"title":"Forget me not, life after un-life","content":"Hey guys, how's things? I had a thought about 2e and I want your opinions on this.<br /> <br /> A concern that I had during the first edition was the issue of the Redeemed and how they are not able to remember their former lives as one of the Created (unless you get an exceptional success on a role). I just remember that as being a cop out. I get that the &quot;goal&quot; of the game is for the Created to reach a Mortal stage, but then just forgetting their journey, the knowledge of the things that exist on the shadows, even their fellow Created, all forgotten. Sometimes to be forgotten by someone who was your throng mate is worse then being rejected.<br /> <br /> Sure, unless they have an Anchor, there's really nothing else to extinguish a Redeemed from a normal human, but I always thought there should be more to tie in this new mortal live to the world of the Created.<br /> <br /> First, they can add a new dimension to the Created's world rather than just being the end result. Like the Fetches in Changeling the Lost and those rare few humans that have high enough willpower, and mortal alchemists, the Redeemed can either be a friend or foe to the Promethean along their journey. <br /> <br /> Secondly, and more importantly IMO, the Created spend much of their time strengthening themselves against those things that bump in the dark, and most know that humans are such fragile creatures; if they can't keep their Transmutations and their supernatural resistance as a mortal, they should at the very least remember their journey and therefore better recognize which darkened ally in the city to avoid. (That's the domain of the city's bloodthirsty vampire Prince.) Nobody wants to spend centuries trying to become human only to be picked off by THE Forsaken pack they once tussled with as a Created in Central Park because they don't remember that as their territory. But the pack does, and they remember the Redeemed as a powerful foe.<br /> <br /> But of course, these are concerns for those players who wish to continue the story after reaching the New Dawn unlike the first reason, having a possible friend or foe, which can be used on a throng still on the path to humanity.<br /> <br /> So, what do ya think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T23:06:22-07:00","id":551146,"title":"","content":"I've mentioned it elsewhere, but I'll repeat it here: there's a disconnect between the mechanics and the flavor text in 1e. According to the mechanics, all but the very lowest-Azoth former Prometheans are virtually guaranteed to regain their memories \u2014 eventually (as in, within a few months). According to the fluff, most Redeemed lose their memories. <br /> <br /> I generally lean more in favor of the mechanics for the sorts of reasons given in KingMe1's post; though I tweak them slightly: as things stand, the fact that you get to try, try again until you either succeed or are reduced to a chance die makes the Final Azoth Roll resemble an extended action \u2014 so I just treat it as an Extended Action (per the new rules, where there's a cap on how many times you get to roll), with most of the penalties replaced by increases to the number of successes needed before you get your memories back. <br /> <br /> In effect, the amnesia becomes a \u201ctransition period\u201d that every Redeemed goes through; and unless you have a low Azoth and a large number of obstacles, it's only a matter of time before you get your memories back. Exceptional Successes speed you on your way and grant you a special benefit (such as immunity to Lunacy, Quiessence, and Disquiet), but don't necessarily end the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T00:04:20-07:00","id":552626,"title":"","content":"You're absolutely right, about the disconnect, the Extended Action and such.<br /> <br /> What I'm talking about is my hope that in the 2Edition, that all Redeemed, UNLESS you have a low Azoth or Humanity (or whatever measure you're using), will automatically remember their former lives . . . and remain immune to Disquiet. Not Lunacy or Disbelief, or whatever, just Disquiet. I believe that aspect would make for a much better game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}